The error message indicates that multipart hashing is not supported, but the function proceeds to perform hashing operations before this check. The check for 'finish' should occur before calling 'pico_sha256_update' to avoid processing data that cannot be completed. Consider moving this check earlier in the function, before line 43.
```suggestion
	if (!finish) {
		LOG_ERR("Multipart hashing not supported yet");
		ret = -ENOTSUP;
		goto end;
	}

	pico_sha256_update(&data->state, pkt->in_buf, pkt->in_len);
```

Missing include for hardware SHA256 definitions. The driver uses hardware-level functions like sha256_wait_valid_blocking, sha256_hw, sha256_err_not_ready_clear, sha256_set_bswap, and sha256_start which are typically defined in hardware/sha256.h from the pico SDK. Add the include after the pico/sha256.h include.
```suggestion
#include <pico/sha256.h>
#include <hardware/sha256.h>
```

The output buffer size is not validated before writing 32 bytes (8 uint32_t values) to it. This could lead to a buffer overflow if pkt->out_buf_max is less than 32 bytes. Add a check to validate that pkt->out_buf_max is at least 32 bytes before writing the hash result.
```suggestion

	if (pkt->out_buf_max < 32) {
		LOG_ERR("Output buffer too small: %u bytes (need at least 32)", pkt->out_buf_max);
		ret = -EINVAL;
		goto end;
	}
```

