When generating FOREACH macros for empty maps (plen == 0), the generated macro definitions will be empty strings, which could result in invalid macro definitions. For example, if there are no entries, `FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY(fn)` would expand to nothing instead of a valid empty expression. Consider generating an appropriate empty value or adding a check to handle the empty case explicitly, similar to how other parts of the code handle empty collections.
```suggestion
        if plen == 0:
            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY(fn)"] = "((void)0)"
            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_SEP(fn, sep)"] = "((void)0)"
            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_VARGS(fn, ...)"] = "((void)0)"
            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_SEP_VARGS(fn, sep, ...)"] = "((void)0)"
        else:
            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY(fn)"] = ' \\\n\t'.join(
                f'fn(DT_{node.z_path_id}, {prop_id}, {i})' for i in range(plen)
            )

            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_SEP(fn, sep)"] = (
                ' DT_DEBRACKET_INTERNAL sep \\\n\t'.join(
                    f'fn(DT_{node.z_path_id}, {prop_id}, {i})' for i in range(plen)
                )
            )

            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_VARGS(fn, ...)"] = ' \\\n\t'.join(
                f'fn(DT_{node.z_path_id}, {prop_id}, {i}, __VA_ARGS__)' for i in range(plen)
            )

            macro2val[f"{macro}_FOREACH_MAP_ENTRY_SEP_VARGS(fn, sep, ...)"] = (
                ' DT_DEBRACKET_INTERNAL sep \\\n\t'.join(
                    f'fn(DT_{node.z_path_id}, {prop_id}, {i}, __VA_ARGS__)' for i in range(plen)
                )
            )
```

