`uart_fifo_read()` can return a negative error (e.g. -ENOSYS/-ENOTSUP). Returning immediately here means RX interrupts may stay pending (no FIFO drain/ack) and the ISR can be retriggered continuously. Consider at least logging the error and disabling RX (and/or draining if possible) to avoid an interrupt storm and a stuck Modbus interface.
